   "table_index": 1,
   "label": "Table 1",
   "caption": "The antimicrobial activity of RNase 7 against common uropathogensTo evaluate the antimicrobial activity of RNase 7 against uropathogenic bacteria, uropathogens were incubated with serial dilutions of recombinant RNase 7 ranging from 0.1–10 μM. Repeat testing was performed on all bacterial isolates in triplicate.",
   "footnotes": [
    "Minimal inhibitory concentration (MIC) necessary to prevent growth of 90% of the bacteria (90% lethal dose [LD90]).",
    "Minimal bactericidal concentration (MBC) necessary to kill ≥99.9% of the bacteria."
